{
  "category": "womens_dresses",
  "version": "0.1",
  "notes": [
    "Every attribute includes 'unknown' so the extractor is never forced to guess.",
    "selection 'single' means exactly one value; 'multi' means a list of zero or more values.",
    "The LLM should omit unsupported attributes; Python should fill missing single attributes with unknown and missing multi attributes with ['unknown'].",
    "Use none only for explicitly supported absence. Never combine unknown, none, or not_applicable with other multi values.",
    "Use not_applicable only when explicit construction makes an attribute inapplicable, such as slit_height when no slit is stated explicitly or adjustable_straps for an explicitly strapless dress.",
    "dress_type describes garment construction; silhouette describes overall shape. A slip dress may also have a bodycon silhouette. Use other when an explicit construction is outside dress_type values; use unknown for a generic dress with no construction details.",
    "Do not infer dress_length from a model's height or a measurement without an explicit length label. High-low length requires explicit uneven front/back lengths or high-low wording.",
    "waist_position locates the waistline; waist_detail describes its construction. An empire waist does not establish overall fit.",
    "Closure is multi to capture combinations. Generic zip or button wording does not establish closure_position.",
    "Straps may coexist with sleeves. Do not equate sleeveless with strapless or infer adjustable straps from their width.",
    "For fabric_type prefer blend for explicitly mixed fibers. Do not infer stretch, opacity, weight, lining, or built-in support from fiber or silhouette alone.",
    "Do not infer solid pattern, secondary color absence, pockets, bra friendliness, or maternity suitability from silence.",
    "Only extract facts about this dress, not styling suggestions or coordinating items. Occasion and style_tags are subjective and best used as soft ranking boosts.",
    "Source category Dresses alone does not verify gender. Apply within the intended womenswear catalog scope.",
    "Start with priority attributes. Preserve source metadata, exact measurements, and fiber percentages separately."
  ],
